{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>And a charmer.</b> Those who say they bind demons." "<b>A necromancer and a knower.</b> I have explained it." "<b>And one who inquires of the dead.</b> Those who go to the cemetery and take a bone of a dead person, and because of their thought and delusion, an image of forms appears to them in dream and even while awake. And all these are abominations to HaShem, for the truth is that the heart of man be always whole with his Creator. And when he leans on his wisdom to seek truth and what will be apart from HaShem — behold, his heart is deficient, for he is corrupted. And whoever wishes to inquire, let him inquire of HaShem through the prophet; therefore it is written after this, \"A prophet from your midst\" — this is Joshua. And the proof that He said to him, \"You shall listen to him,\" and it is written, \"And the children of Israel listened to him.\" And yet another proof: we have not found a prophet who entered with Israel into the land except Joshua. Also possible is that this is a general statement for every prophet who arises after Moses."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:23:56.459781808Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}